<p>The <em>Common Lexical Translations</em> specification provides reusable lexical categories and
translation rules. These rules describe how sequences of Unicode code points are recognized,
transformed, and classified as words, and are reused by language specifications within
<em>Michael Heilmann's Arcadia</em>.</p>
<p>Each consuming language defines its own complete lexical grammar, including its start symbol,
word alternatives, and ambiguity-resolution rules. This specification supplies the common building
blocks, not a universal word production.</p>
